  "rationale": "Every exfiltrate technique requires admin on db, fileserver or backup. Getting a foothold on any of those requires stolen_dbadmin, whose only sources are dump_dbadmin_dc (needs admin_dc) and dump_dbadmin_adfs (needs admin_adfs). Those in turn need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which only auth_dc and auth_adfs provide. Both require NOT mfa_admin, and the deployed mfa:admin defence makes mfa_admin true, so both are blocked. The attacker can still reach the internal network, appserver and apiserver and can steal admin credentials via kerberoasting, but cannot obtain stolen_dbadmin. Exfiltration is therefore unreachable."
